# A11yForge – HTTP Client (IntelliJ)
# Ausfuehren: gruener Pfeil links neben dem Request.
# Reihenfolge: zuerst Register (einmalig) -> Login (setzt {{token}}) -> Rest.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Register (einmalig)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "max@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "userName": "max"
}

### Login -> speichert Token in globale Variable
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "max@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Logout
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Scan starten (projectId anpassen)
POST {{host}}/api/scan
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": 1
}

### Scan abrufen (id anpassen)
GET {{host}}/api/scan/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Projekte auflisten
GET {{host}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pages auflisten
GET {{host}}/api/pages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Violations auflisten
GET {{host}}/api/violations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Fix-Generierung anstossen (violationId anpassen) -> 202 Accepted
POST {{host}}/api/fix-proposals
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "violationId": 1
}

### Fix-Proposal abrufen (id anpassen)
GET {{host}}/api/fix-proposals/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
